Title: Gaze never reports a failed plan check as passing
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-27T13:38Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Raid 2026-10-27: on PR #1768 gaze posted `plan check: PASS with deviations` while `seat_clock.py
plan-check` had returned FAIL (a free-text manifest the checker cannot parse, plus a stale `.status`
from a refused seat); the verify-gate of #1768 took the line at face value. The same malformed-manifest
FAIL appeared in at least four other gaze runs today (#1742, #1751, #1755, #1756), each time hand-edited
or rewritten after the fact. A review that reports a failed check as passing corrupts the review record.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Gaze copies the plan check's verdict verbatim into the result (a script writes the line, not the
      model); a FAIL can be followed by a stated reason, never relabelled PASS.
- [ ] The plan manifest is written by a helper (or validated at write time), so the free-text format
      that the checker cannot parse cannot be produced.
- [ ] A test: a FAIL from the checker yields a result comment whose plan-check line says FAIL.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
skills/gaze/SKILL.md, skills/gaze/references/output.md, skills/gaze/references/plan.md, scripts/seat_clock.py, scripts/gaze_close.py
